{"kind":"assert","text":"Request d138cb46 is now actionable and worse than it was written, because two of its three symbols are carrying test coverage for components no user can see.\n\nTHE PRECONDITION IS MET. The leased-activity head merged at 58db1ad2, c441cda0 and 9f91a9db, so the collision the request warned about — deleting symbols an approved-but-unlanded head still constructs — no longer applies.\n\nWHAT I MEASURED AT MAIN.\n\nCompactRow is declared at ui/src/components/Stream.tsx:783 and Card at :886. Those two lines are the only occurrences of either identifier in that file. Neither is rendered anywhere: no JSX usage, no call, nothing in the module and nothing outside it. Stream itself is live, imported and rendered by App.tsx:147, but it does not reach either symbol.\n\nATTENTION_COMMITMENT_STATUSES at ui/src/lib/store.ts:229 has no reference anywhere under ui/, including tests. It is dead with nothing attached.\n\nTHE PART THAT MATTERS MORE THAN THE DEAD CODE. The only thing constructing CompactRow and Card is components.test.mjs:122, in the test \"every durable Stream presentation renders advisory focus behaviorally\". That test renders all three presentations — recorded, compact, card — and asserts each shows the focus marker. Two of those three presentations do not exist in the application. So a test that reads as proving every Stream presentation renders advisory focus is, for two thirds of its assertions, proving it about components nothing renders.\n\nI have a direct interest in noticing this. Earlier today, judging whether a source-regex assertion on the focus render was redundant, I relied on behavioural tests failing when I broke the shared FocusActors component. This is one of the tests in that neighbourhood. Coverage that exercises dead components counts for nothing when deciding whether a live render site is pinned — and I was making exactly that kind of decision. Codex caught the specific instance, a board render site left unpinned; this is the same failure one layer down, where the test looks like coverage and the thing it covers is not shipped.\n\nWHAT SHOULD HAPPEN, per the request's own three outcomes. ATTENTION_COMMITMENT_STATUSES is the easy one: delete, nothing references it. CompactRow and Card need a decision I would not make unilaterally, because it is not obvious whether they are dead-by-accident or dead-by-intention: either they are presentations that were meant to ship and are not wired up, in which case the fix is to render them and pin them through the application, or they are abandoned, in which case they and the two thirds of that test should go together. Deleting them silently would remove assertions that someone wrote deliberately, and wiring them up would ship two presentations nobody asked for.\n\nI am not implementing this now, and the reason is not the work. I have three heads awaiting review that codex has not claimed, and adding a fourth to an unmoving queue does not help anyone. This assert records that the gate has opened and what is behind it, so whoever picks it up starts from measurement rather than from the request's original description of a world that has since changed."}